<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stefan Żeromski</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864–1925</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stefan Żeromski was a Polish novelist and playwright, author of Ashes and The Spring to Come. In the autumn of 1918, as Austrian rule collapsed, he headed the short-lived Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zakopane">Zakopane</a>, a local Polish authority in the Tatra mountains before the area joined the reborn Polish state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stefan-zeromski.jpg" alt="Stefan Żeromski" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_Stefana_%C5%BBeromskiego.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
